   "widgets": [
    {
     "tabId": "1f7894ac-ab74-4751-af11-c7efb5624f3a",
     "id": "26c2158a-22cf-4afb-b182-f98ac9c2cc43",
     "type": "TextDisplay",
     "title": "How to read this",
     "collapsed": false,
     "state": "",
     "height": 0,
     "gridsterCoords": {
      "x": 1,
      "y": 1,
      "w": 12,
      "h": 5
     },
     "config": {
      "description": "\n<h3>Network rapid &mdash; is a NIC or link bad right now?</h3>\n<p>This screen catches <b>grey-state failure</b>: partial degradation that\nleaves everything nominally up. A NIC dropping 0.1% of frames still moves\ntraffic at line rate, so throughput and latency look green through the exact\nfault this exists to find. <b>Non-zero is the catch.</b> It is not a\nroot-cause tool.</p>\n<p><b>Drop and pause metrics are per-mille, not percent.</b> A value of\n<code>1</code> means 0.1%, which is already Broadcom's warning threshold for\nout-of-order packets; <code>10</code> is critical. Do not read them as packet\ncounts.</p>\n<p><b>RX missed errors</b> means the NIC ring buffer had no free descriptor and\nthe packet was dropped before the driver saw it &mdash; distinct from\n<i>RX dropped</i> (discarded higher up) and <i>RX errors</i> (arrived damaged).\nIt is the clearest signal that a NIC is being overrun.</p>\n<p><b>Pause / PFC</b> separate a congested fabric from a failing NIC: the host\nasking the switch to slow down is a different problem from the host losing\nframes.</p>\n<p><b>Blind spot:</b> there are no disk media-error counters anywhere in the\nvSAN Performance Service, and no NIC ring-buffer <i>utilisation</i> &mdash;\nonly overflow after the fact. A green screen here does not mean the hardware is\nhealthy.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/nickfirefoot/vsanhostmetrics\">Documentation and\nfull metric reference</a></p>\n",
      "locationUrl": "",
      "locationFile": "",
      "viewModeHTML": true,
      "refreshInterval": 300,
      "widgetId": "26c2158a-22cf-4afb-b182-f98ac9c2cc43",
      "title": "How to read this",
      "refreshContent": {
       "refreshContent": false
      },
      "viewDetails": ""
     }
    },
